            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "Thanks — I had validated only the checked-in catalog. I have now rebased, built with `ENABLE_TRANSLATIONS=ON`, and run the official `update-po-zh_TW.UTF-8` target. The active catalog now matches the generated POT (2,086/2,086 msgids, up from 1,343), and `E5200` has a reviewed zh-TW translation with its placeholder preserved. Strict `msgfmt` and the translation build pass. Newly surfaced untranslated/fuzzy entries remain explicitly incomplete rather than being machine-translated. This refresh is generated from Neovim sources; I would not port it directly to Vim because its catalog and message set should be updated and reviewed separately.",
